# Local HTML preview after Cursor restart

Alex works on HubSpot/homepage HTML files in this repo (`OurERP_1.html`, `home6.html`, `home7.html`, etc.). After every Cursor app restart (and at the start of a session when he is editing HTML), he needs a **working link preview** without having to ask.

## Standing behavior

1. Identify the HTML file he is actively working on this session (open editor tab, recent edits, or the file named in the latest request). Prefer that file over older ones.
2. Ensure a local static server is serving the repo root. Prefer port **5500** (historical Live Server port). If 5500 is free, start one; if something already serves the repo on 5500, reuse it.
3. Immediately give him a clickable preview URL in **exactly this format** (same pattern he already uses):
   - `http://localhost:5500/OurERP_1.html`
   - `http://localhost:5500/home7.html`
   - `http://localhost:5500/<ActiveFile>.html`
   Never substitute a different host, port, path style, or file-tree index URL unless 5500 truly cannot be used.
4. Do this proactively when resuming after reboot / new chat / new session on homepage HTML work — do not wait for him to ask for “the link again.”
5. If the server died (port empty, connection refused), restart it and re-share the same URL pattern.

## How to start the server (Windows / this repo)

From the repo root `C:\Users\amcintyre\Projects\FUNDVIEW_Home` (or the home clone path). Prefer the repo preview server — it disables caching and auto-reloads HTML after save:

```powershell
node _preview_server.js 5500
```

One-click alternative: double-click `start-preview.cmd` in the repo root (opens `http://localhost:5500/OurERP_1.html`).

Fallback once `%APPDATA%\npm` exists:

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "$env:APPDATA\npm" | Out-Null
npx --yes serve -l 5500 .
```

Run it in the background. Confirm the port is listening before pasting the link.

**Stale preview guard:** Always serve the dual-mode source file (e.g. `OurERP_1.html`), never the `.hubspot.html` export. Prefer `_preview_server.js` so Cache-Control is `no-store` and the page live-reloads on save.

## Notes

- Local preview uses the dual-mode source file (e.g. `OurERP_1.html`), **not** the `.hubspot.html` export.
- Keep this habit for whichever HTML page is the session focus, not only OurERP.
